    {
      "id": "213df2ed-8913-4a61-a366-c1230370b733",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -656,
        -720
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 560,
        "height": 920,
        "content": "## 09-01-01 revive quiet client projects with AI check-in emails\n\n### How it works\n\nFreelancers and small studios lose projects in silence, not in conflict. This workflow runs every Monday morning: it reads the Client Projects table in Airtable, counts how many days since the last touchpoint on every active project, and picks the ones quiet for 10 days or more. For each quiet project an AI assistant writes a short, human check-in email that mentions the project and its stage and invites the client to raise anything. The email goes out by Gmail, the send is logged to the Touch Log table, the project last_touch is updated so it is not flagged again next week, and Discord gets a one line summary. If nothing is quiet, Discord gets an all clear. Rows with broken data get flagged to the ops inbox instead of failing silently. Every Friday a digest email and Discord post summarize project health: how many are healthy, how many went quiet this week and which ones are past 30 days of silence.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Create an Airtable base with a Client Projects table (project_id, project_name, client_name, client_email, stage, owner_email, last_touch, status) and a Touch Log table (log_id, project_id, project_name, client_name, client_email, stage, days_quiet, ai_subject, ai_body, sent_at, run_date).\n- Fill Client Projects with your active projects and set last_touch to the date of your last real contact.\n- Connect Airtable, Gmail and Discord webhook credentials on the matching nodes.\n- Adjust the quiet threshold (10 days) in the spawn code node and the two schedules to your week.\n\n### Customization\n\nChange the quiet threshold or the stages that count as active, swap Discord for Slack, or route the digest to Telegram."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
